      "worked_solution": "Recall the definition of tangent: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡P=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{QR}{PQ}=\\frac{QR}{3.5}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing length $QR.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QR & =\\sqrt{P{R}^{2}-P{Q}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12.5}^{2}-{3.5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{156.25-12.25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡P & =\\frac{QR}{3.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{35} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
